title: Code fences
warnings: 0
sections: 7

[1] id=code-fences anchor=code-fences lines=1-10
heading: Code fences
| Text before the fences.
|
| ```sh
| # not a heading
| ## still not a heading
| echo done
| ```

[2] id=after-backticks anchor=after-backticks lines=11-17
heading: After backticks
| ~~~python
| # comment, not a heading
| def f(): pass
| ~~~

[3] id=longer-fence anchor=longer-fence lines=18-27
heading: Longer fence
| ````markdown
| # Fake title inside a four-backtick fence
| ```
| nested three-backtick fence does not close it
| ```
| ## Fake section
| ````

[4] id=mixed-markers anchor=mixed-markers lines=28-35
heading: Mixed markers
| ```
| # the tilde line below does not close a backtick fence
| ~~~
| # still inside the code
| ```

[5] id=indented-fence anchor=indented-fence lines=36-45
heading: Indented fence
|   ```text
|   # two spaces of indentation are allowed
|   ```
|
|     ```
|     # indented code block, so this is not a fence
|     ```

[6] id=inline-triple-backticks anchor=inline-triple-backticks lines=46-51
heading: Inline triple backticks
| ```inline``` at the start of a line is not a fence.
|
| Use ```inline``` triple backticks inside a paragraph.

[7] id=end anchor=end lines=52-54
heading: End
| Last section.
